MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace `verimark_run_capture_match_pipeline` (and its enclosing
`verimark_verify` / `verimark_identify` vfuncs) with a 32-state
`fpi_ssm` that drives every Tudor opcode through
`verimark_session_call_opcode_async` (Phase 10.3.b foundation).

Why : the sync pipeline blocked the libfprint GMainLoop for up to
30 s × 3 = 90 s during the 0x87 polling cycle, exceeding the 25 s
DBus reply deadline that fprintd-CLI enforces on VerifyStart and
freezing Ctrl+C / VerifyStop until the poll returned.

Architecture :
- Per-opcode states (`VFY_S_PRE_*`, `VFY_S_DRAIN_*`, `VFY_S_CFG_*`,
  `VFY_S_POLL_*`, `VFY_S_MATCH`, `VFY_S_POST_*`, `VFY_S_RESOLVE_*`).
- Poll loop = state pair `POLL_READ` / `POLL_WAIT` re-fired every
  250 ms via `g_timeout_add` until frame_ready, false-detect
  (RICH only), or the per-attempt 30 s deadline.
- Inter-attempt sleep 500 ms = `VFY_S_DRAIN_SLEEP` via `g_timeout_add`.
- 4 shared async callbacks : `vfy_cb_advance` (default, ignores
  status + payload), `vfy_cb_evread_poll` (parses 0x87 events,
  decides frame_ready / false_detect / continue),
  `vfy_cb_match` (status 0x0000 + payload ≥ 16 B = MATCH),
  `vfy_cb_resolve` (stashes 0xa0 02 storage_handle for the done cb).
- Verify ↔ identify share one SSM ; `verify_sm_done` dispatches
  on `fpi_device_get_current_action()` (verify : compare resolved
  handle vs requested print, downgrade FAIL if mismatch ;
  identify : look up resolved handle in fprintd's gallery).
- `GCancellable` from `fpi_device_get_cancellable()` is wired into
  every async opcode → Ctrl+C / VerifyStop now propagate cleanly
  via `G_IO_ERROR_CANCELLED`.
- Defensive timer cleanup in `verify_sm_done` (`g_source_remove`
  if `pending_timer_id != 0`) — even though the harness shouldn't
  let stale timers fire on a dead SSM, the asymmetric ownership
  with `fpi_ssm_set_data` makes the safety net cheap.

The `verify` and `identify` vfuncs become 5-line trampolines
calling `verimark_run_verify_ssm`. The old sync helpers
(`verimark_verify_drain_between_attempts`, `verimark_run_capture_match_pipeline`)
are removed — no remaining in-tree caller.

Builds clean against libfprint 1.94.10 / libgusb 0.4.9 / GLib 2.86
on NixOS. 11 standalone TDD suites (proto / crypto / tls / pairing /
session / handshake / storage / capture / match / enroll /
bootstrap) stay green — the SSM is in verimark.c gated behind
`VERIMARK_HAVE_LIBGUSB`, invisible to the standalone build.

Runtime validation via `fprintd-verify` / `fprintd-list` /
`fprintd-identify` against the real sensor pending — risk-graded
medium-high since the verify pipeline orchestration is large.

AI-assisted.
